WEBVTT

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:08.770
<b>Meiji Tokyo Renka</b>

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:55.850
Let's go.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:11.510
I heard that Mei-chan can 
hear ghosts talking.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:12.400
Did you know?

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.650
Apparently, that girl can see ghosts.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:16.240
Whoa, really?

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:21.190
You're Ayazuki Mei-san, right?

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:22.510
Do you wanna come with us?

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.410
Mei-chan.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:26.200
Mei-chan!

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:50.810
What was that about?

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:04.370
<b>Meiji Tokyo Renka</b>

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.900
I will be going then, Rintaro-san.

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:16.720
Be sure to look over all 
of them closely.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:20.370
Oh?

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:24.330
Who is this young lady?

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:26.450
The Little Squirrel.

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:27.960
Little Squirrel?

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:31.840
She is the fiancée I was 
telling you about earlier.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:33.620
<i>She</i> is?!

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:38.560
You cannot be serious, Rintaro-san.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:40.590
I am.

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:46.460
Of all the selfish—!

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:50.210
Do you have any understanding of your 
position as the eldest son of the Mori family?

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:53.080
Marrying such a lowly girl as this...!

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.090
L-Lowly girl?

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.340
Listen to me.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:58.710
You will choose a suitable partner

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:01.800
from the selection of pictures 
I brought you, Rintaro-san.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:07.050
There is no other woman more suited 
for the Mori family than her, Aunt.

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:11.810
I will not accept this little girl!

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:13.020
Little girl...

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:30.620
I am sorry about that.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:34.620
It seems that my aunt has heard about 
me declaring you my fiancée

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:36.670
at the Rokumeikan a few days ago.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:41.730
Yesterday and today she came to the 
mansion with matchmaking photos.

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:43.530
Matchmaking photos?

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:47.330
So that's who your unfortunate 
visitor was yesterday.

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:51.970
Unfortunately, I am expecting 
a visitor this evening.

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:56.700
Your aunt will probably come again 
tomorrow from the sounds of it.

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:59.060
Well, about that...

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:02.900
A party will be held next month 
at the Rokumeikan, and key people

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:04.570
from various circles will be there.

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:09.210
I would like to formally present 
you as my fiancée there.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.740
Formally present?

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:12.490
Fiancée?

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:15.110
Wha?! Formally present me?!

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:21.720
You can't. That's the grand event 
nobles and government officials will be at.

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:24.650
You would be making a fool of yourself.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:28.590
Don't worry. It will be fine.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:43.230
<b>Flower of Asakusa Rendezvous</b>

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:00.490
<i>Formally present me as his fiancée...</i>

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:04.770
That is how he is protecting you.

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:09.720
Little Squirrel.

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:19.790
Why don't you join me for a bit?

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:22.630
Eh?

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:40.670
U-Umm... Where are we going?

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:42.330
To an enjoyable place.

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:43.020
Eh?

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:47.660
Are you familiar with 
the flower of Asakusa?

00:06:48.890 --> 00:06:52.420
Asakusa? Yes, I am!

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.600
I don't know this Asakusa...

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:07.920
Hey now! Don't just stand 
there spacing out, ya idiot!

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:10.040
S-Sorry!

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:13.660
We should probably hold hands 
so you don't get lost.

00:07:14.670 --> 00:07:16.660
O-Okay...

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:30.920
<b>Picture
 Postcards</b>

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:34.450
Apparently, they're selling 
picture postcards.

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:37.170
All these people are here 
for picture postcards?

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:40.930
I'll take this one.

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:43.360
And this one, and this one.

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:44.850
I'll take them all!

00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:49.190
That's so unfair, Higuchi-san. 
Buying up just Kawakami-san's pictures...

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:53.000
A heart ardently in love is 
as precious as the divine.

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:54.820
Otojiro-sama!

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:07.080
Now I see. All these people are here because 
they're after Kawakami Otojiro-kun's actor photos.

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:09.260
Kawakami Otojiro?

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:12.460
You met him at the Rokumeikan, remember?

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:16.490
He is a handsome actor who is 
extremely popular right now.

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:18.890
At the Rokumeikan?

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:20.600
Kawakami Otojiro...

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:23.350
W-What?

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:27.120
Do you really not remember 
meeting a handsome man

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:30.860
with scores of women in love with him?

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:35.990
Not really. I met a lot of people 
for the first time that day.

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:40.540
Ah, well, it just so happens that today he 
has a performance at the Tokiwa Theater.

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:42.440
We'll go see it later.

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:45.020
We're going to see a play?

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:47.950
Yes, but before we do that...

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:54.490
This ice cream is very popular right now.

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:57.770
I thought you might like it.

00:08:57.770 --> 00:09:01.410
Yes! Yes! Yes! I love it!

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:04.510
So sweet!

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:09.100
Cold! Sweet! Cold!

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:12.380
My, you got some on your face.

00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:19.670
The perfect amount of sweetness.

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:24.860
Your ice cream is dripping, Little Squirrel.

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:28.040
What a waste!

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:34.170
<b>Enami Photography Studio</b>

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:43.170
Miss, your expression is a bit too stiff.

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:47.520
I-I heard that photographs in this 
time period were really expensive.

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:48.870
This time period?

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:52.180
U-Umm... How much does this cost?

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:55.440
Ah, well, one photograph is 16 yen.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:56.650
So cheap!

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:58.020
I mean...

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:01.950
Then, how does that convert into sukiyaki?

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:03.220
Huh?

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:05.720
You could buy 320 bowls of sukiyaki.

00:10:07.030 --> 00:10:09.050
T-That much?!

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:12.510
I accidentally took the picture.
 That will be 16 yen.

00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:14.890
You're so cute, Little Squirrel.

00:10:20.690 --> 00:10:23.260
Amazing. It's a full house.

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:26.720
Kawakami Otojiro-san really must be popular.

00:10:27.130 --> 00:10:29.840
So, what kind of play is this?

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:32.890
It is <i>The Golden Demon</i> by Ozaki Kouyou.

00:10:32.890 --> 00:10:37.900
Huh, I feel like I've 
heard of that before...

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:41.420
It was recently serialized in the newspaper.

00:10:41.420 --> 00:10:43.950
Have you read it, Little Squirrel?

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:46.750
No, I don't know what it's about.

00:10:47.090 --> 00:10:50.260
It is a love-hate play depicting a tragic
 relationship between a man and a woman.

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:54.000
So it's not going to have 
a happy ending, then.

00:10:55.270 --> 00:10:58.870
A happy ending? I'm surprised you 
would use English so casually.

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:02.640
Are you perhaps familiar with 
foreign plays, Little Squirrel?

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:04.730
No, not at all.

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:07.340
The only foreign plays I know about are...

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:12.390
Uhh... Just <i>Romeo and Juliet</i>, I guess.

00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:15.330
Oh, that's impressive.

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:17.140
Isn't that by Shakespeare?

00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:19.010
Shakespeare...

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:22.410
A-And I believe he also wrote <i>Hamlet</i>.

00:11:23.030 --> 00:11:27.160
"To be or not to be, that is the question."

00:11:28.010 --> 00:11:32.710
Shouldn't it be, "To live or not 
to live, that is the question,"

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:35.510
or something?

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:38.370
So that's how you translated that passage?

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:41.410
I-I didn't exactly translate it.

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:47.060
You replaced "to be" with "to live" 
and "not to be" with "not to live."

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:50.500
And I believe the passage after that is, 
"to die, to sleep,"

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:54.250
which means that to die is to sleep, 
so that is a very natural translation.

00:11:54.250 --> 00:11:56.300
In fact, it's quite reasonable.

00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:58.520
You are incredible, Little Squirrel!

00:11:58.520 --> 00:11:59.830
Uh, sure.

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:04.430
Just how much must you
impress me before you're content?

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:06.090
U-Um...

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:09.570
I'm grateful that you're pleased.

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:19.110
A diamond!

00:12:19.110 --> 00:12:20.980
That is a diamond!

00:12:20.980 --> 00:12:26.600
That is the 300 yen diamond that 
has captivated the heart of Omiya!

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:30.040
Three hundred yen for a diamond? That's cheap.

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:32.840
That's worth about sixty million bowls of sukiyaki.

00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:33.860
T-That's so expensive!

00:12:35.340 --> 00:12:37.660
Having been dazzled by a diamond,

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:43.180
Omiya chooses a rich suitor instead 
of her childhood friend Kanichi.

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:46.780
Our play begins with a disturbance 
along the beach of Atami.

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:49.620
What will the fate of these two people be?

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:54.090
Otojiro-san!

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:56.020
Otojiro-sama!

00:13:00.110 --> 00:13:01.970
That man...

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:07.140
You went through all this just because 
you wanted to dance with me, didn't you?

00:13:10.090 --> 00:13:11.480
That was him!

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:15.630
Kan'ichi-san! I... I...

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:20.880
I will never forget the moon 
on this night, even if I die.

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:25.220
And on this night next year,
 the year after that,

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:28.690
and even ten years from now,

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:33.030
the moon will surely be 
clouded with my tears.

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:41.720
<i>On this night next year, huh?</i>

00:13:42.140 --> 00:13:44.920
<i>Where will I be when that comes?</i>

00:13:53.590 --> 00:13:57.470
I can't believe there are buildings 
this tall in Asakusa.

00:13:57.470 --> 00:13:59.980
Looks like it was a good 
idea to have you come out,

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:01.760
rather than staying stuck 
inside the mansion.

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:08.820
I thought the various stimuli 
might help you regain your memories.

00:14:10.060 --> 00:14:11.640
<i>He did this for me?</i>

00:14:12.110 --> 00:14:14.320
Umm, I...

00:14:14.630 --> 00:14:16.610
It's fine. Take your time.

00:14:16.610 --> 00:14:22.210
You are always welcome to stay at the 
mansion as you are now, if you'd like.

00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:29.590
Now, let us go have the 
most exceptional lunch.

00:14:31.950 --> 00:14:32.910
Okay!

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:50.220
This beefsteak is so good!

00:14:52.470 --> 00:14:53.690
What is it?

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:58.940
I'm impressed by how skillfully 
you use the knife and fork.

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:01.290
Really?

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:03.550
I think I'm pretty average.

00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:05.230
Take a look around you.

00:15:06.530 --> 00:15:09.560
You eat the meat by piercing 
it with this rake.

00:15:10.750 --> 00:15:15.230
Ouch! I stabbed the inside of my mouth!

00:15:19.720 --> 00:15:21.720
This soup is delicious.

00:15:23.260 --> 00:15:27.290
Table manners are not something 
that are mastered in a day.

00:15:27.290 --> 00:15:31.990
And with that Shakespeare comment from 
before, you are truly a mysterious girl.

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:33.450
Mysterious?

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:38.000
I guess so.

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:42.010
I am sure you will be able to 
handle the formal presentation.

00:15:42.010 --> 00:15:43.810
The formal presentation?

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:46.960
N-No way, I can't!

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.140
Why not?

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:52.430
You are fond of Shakespeare,
 you have mastered Western table manners,

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:57.600
and you enjoy food without hesitation.
That makes you perfect.

00:15:57.620 --> 00:15:59.400
I-I'm not so sure...

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:02.980
Believe in yourself.

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:07.110
You just need to remember your usual smile.

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:09.390
Now, eat up, eat up.

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:11.570
Okay, I will.

00:16:18.030 --> 00:16:20.230
It's so good!

00:16:35.380 --> 00:16:36.940
S-Sor— Sor— Sor—!

00:16:36.940 --> 00:16:43.310
Well, well. What an unexpected 
surprise, Mori-sensei.

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:45.360
Eh? Eh?

00:16:46.430 --> 00:16:48.430
It is, Arima-san.

00:16:48.430 --> 00:16:52.080
I have not seen you since 
Senju's poetry party.

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:58.840
My daughter has been eagerly 
awaiting an invitation from you.

00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:01.840
Shino, say hello.

00:17:01.840 --> 00:17:02.780
Of course.

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:10.460
It has been quite some time. I am Shino.

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:14.210
It has indeed. I am pleased 
to see you are doing well.

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:18.220
And who would this young 
lady be, Mori-sensei?

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:25.220
My fiancée.

00:17:25.220 --> 00:17:26.740
Fiancée?

00:17:27.640 --> 00:17:31.740
Then... the rumors of your 
engagement are true?

00:17:33.590 --> 00:17:36.230
Indeed they are true.

00:17:38.490 --> 00:17:40.330
Pardon my rudeness,

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:43.500
but which noble family 
are you the daughter of?

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:46.510
She is not from any noble family.

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:51.000
You are planning to marry a commoner?

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:54.630
Yes. I was not attracted by her pedigree,

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:58.270
but rather by her soul.

00:17:59.750 --> 00:18:01.770
Is that right?

00:18:02.780 --> 00:18:08.490
Well, then, congratulations on such 
a well-mannered young lady.

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:10.730
Have a pleasant day.

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:15.600
Shall we get back to eating?

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:44.300
Hey, you.

00:18:49.820 --> 00:18:52.070
Was it that bad?

00:18:52.070 --> 00:18:53.230
Huh?

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:54.830
The beefsteak.

00:18:54.830 --> 00:18:57.090
Oh, not at all.

00:18:57.090 --> 00:18:59.270
It was incredibly good.

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:02.570
We should've invited you to come with us.

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:07.690
No, I'm not really familiar 
with formal table manners.

00:19:07.690 --> 00:19:11.570
I wouldn't want to bring shame on Ougai-san.

00:19:14.820 --> 00:19:17.680
I ended up bringing shame on him.

00:19:19.710 --> 00:19:21.860
<i>She was so pretty.</i>

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:25.480
<i>I wouldn't stand a chance against her.</i>

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:31.730
Do I seem even a little bit like 
I should be Ougai-san's fiancée?

00:19:35.620 --> 00:19:39.080
He was the youngest person to 
graduate from medical school.

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:39.660
Huh?

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:42.820
He studied abroad in Germany 
at government expense,

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:47.620
and much is expected of him in 
the future as an army official.

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:50.490
Moreover, he is highly valued 
in the literary world.

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:53.250
Ougai-san.

00:19:54.260 --> 00:19:59.260
If such an incredible person is saying 
you're fine, isn't that enough?

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:00.330
What?

00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:05.050
In your case, no matter what 
unreasonable demands you make,

00:20:05.050 --> 00:20:08.520
I can tell that, unexpectedly, you have
 the fighting spirit to see things through.

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:10.250
Syunso-san...

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:14.730
Anyway, will you please stop doing that?

00:20:52.510 --> 00:20:54.400
The more I look at everything...

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:58.550
Watching the river flow,

00:20:58.550 --> 00:21:04.840
The strike of Shinonome...

00:21:05.670 --> 00:21:09.460
You dropped your handkerchief, Miss.

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:14.500
Thank you for picking it up, 
but that is not mine.

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:16.510
My, pardon my rudeness.

00:21:16.510 --> 00:21:18.840
To apologize for my mistake, 
will you join me for tea?

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:19.830
Excuse me?

00:21:20.190 --> 00:21:25.060
Of course I would not mind if we go to 
a normal tea house or a romantic tea house.

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:28.470
What are you doing with your hand?

00:21:29.350 --> 00:21:33.260
Sir, you really shouldn't 
underestimate a geisha.

00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:37.450
And get lost.

00:21:37.450 --> 00:21:39.300
Oh, no. My nails.

00:21:45.630 --> 00:21:49.620
Huh? Haven't I seen you somewhere before?

00:21:50.390 --> 00:21:51.550
Excuse me...

00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:55.130
Please make me into a woman!

00:21:55.130 --> 00:21:56.670
Huh?

00:22:01.350 --> 00:22:02.890
You must have a reason.

00:22:03.590 --> 00:22:06.330
All right then. Follow me.

00:22:09.320 --> 00:22:10.280
Okay!

00:22:14.150 --> 00:22:15.860
My name is Otoyakko.

00:22:15.860 --> 00:22:18.050
Otoyakko-san! What a wonderful name!

00:22:18.050 --> 00:22:19.520
You've got some spunk.

00:22:19.520 --> 00:22:21.920
I was amazed when you asked 
me to make you a woman.

00:22:21.920 --> 00:22:22.990
Thank you very much!

00:22:22.990 --> 00:22:24.710
I wasn't exactly praising you.

00:22:25.040 --> 00:22:26.860
You are such a strange girl.

00:22:26.860 --> 00:22:28.800
Yes, I get that a lot.

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Meiji Tokyo Renka</b>

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:39.970
Next Episode Preview

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:39.970
Long Road to Becoming a Fiancée

00:23:30.300 --> 00:23:31.560
Come on now!

00:23:31.560 --> 00:23:33.380
